rbolt IP) and causes catastrophic kernel panics if packets drop.\\n3. **The Breakthrough Hacker Reality — RDMA over Thunderbolt 5 (Apple Technote TN3205):** Starting in macOS 26.2, Apple introduced native **RDMA (Remote Direct Memory Access) over Thunderbolt 5** for Apple Silicon Macs equipped with Thunderbolt 5 ports (e.g., M4 Pro / M4 Max Mac mini and MacBook Pro). Enabled in macOS Recovery via `rdma_ctl enable`, this bypasses the standard TCP/IP network stack, dropping interconnect latency from ~300 µs to ~3–5 µs at 50–80 Gbps. It does not merge OS-level RAM for general applications, but it enables **shared memory pooling for dist\n<truncated 20740 bytes>","Recipient":"\"1b146f06-0d46-4922-b656-a59fd584eb61\"","toolAction":"\"Sending report to parent\"","toolSummary":"\"Send complete research findings to parent\""}}],"truncated_fields":["tool_calls"]}
